KaiT2en-NixOS divergence: take the AirDrop port only from the AirDrop SRV.

handle_frame() checked the record name for the PTR of the service
(AIRDROP_PTR_NAME, the compressed _airdrop._tcp.local) but took the port
from *any* SRV record in the same frame, last one wins. An Apple device
advertises many services over AWDL, so the port usually belonged to one
of the others -- the port of an unrelated service on the same host.

Sending it back out gets this right already: service_records() names the
SRV `<instance>` + AIRDROP_PTR_NAME. Only the parse was missing the
check.

What it looked like, an iPhone 15 over four hours on one MAC. The
drifting ports are another service's ephemeral ports, 8770 is the real
AirDrop one on the few frames whose last SRV was AirDrop's:

  58988  58990  58991  58993  58996  58998  59000  59002  59011  59013
  49784  62144  and 8770 four times

Every attempt against a wrong port connected, completed the TLS
handshake, had its POST /Discover ACKed, and was then met with silence
until the read timed out: the service on that port is not AirDrop and
has no idea what /Discover is. That reads exactly like a receiver
refusing an unidentified sender, which is what the CLI then reported,
and it is why sending looked broken while receiving worked. The four
frames that did carry 8770 resolved in about three seconds.

Applied by apps/t2-drop/package.nix on top of the upstream source
(-p1 relative to apps/t2-drop).

Drop condition: remove when upstream matches the SRV record to the
AirDrop service name. Re-check every sync.

--- a/src/awdl.rs
+++ b/src/awdl.rs
@@ -364,7 +364,10 @@ impl Awdl {
                             if let Some(label) = first_label(data) {
                                 instance = Some(label);
                             }
-                        } else if kind == DNS_SRV && data.len() >= 6 {
+                        } else if kind == DNS_SRV
+                            && name.ends_with(&AIRDROP_PTR_NAME)
+                            && data.len() >= 6
+                        {
                             airdrop = Some(u16::from_be_bytes([data[4], data[5]]));
                         }
                     }
